            },
            "createdOn": 1774016690,
            "author": {
                "name": "Alexander",
                "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                "username": "pointbazaar"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "As a note, this is fine.  std::regex is widely known to be slow.  There's probably a bunch of articles you could cite, but I'm not worried about it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "isalnum is different than what was there previously, as it calls through locale.  from the cpp reference page (with emphasis for effect)\n\"In the DEFAULT locale, the following characters are alphanumeric:\"\n\nhow often do people change their locale?  Idk, but if the goal is performance, I think being explicit would be better.\n\nSomething trivial like:\n\n```\n{\n    return (c >= '0' && c <= '9') ||\n           (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z') ||\n           (c >= 'a' && c <= 'z');\n};\n```\n\nIs likely going to beat any locale implementation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, this is a tradeoff with relying on defaults / re-implementing for more reliable solutions.\n\nChanged it to your solution which will be stable against locale changes and probably have better performance \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do you need this check?  This should arguably be an error, not silently solve a caller bug?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed the check. Not returning any error since the existing code did not do that either and changing all the callers would cause scope creep.\n\nAdded the assumption (non-empty input) to the function's documentation comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "could we just invert the bool on isValidDBusPathSegmentChar and avoid std::not_fn?  That makes the code simpler"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I find it clearer this way because the function aligns with D-Bus spec which is worded positively. I don't expect any runtime overhead from writing it this way as compared to inverting it in the function itself.\n\nLong-term i would like to put functions like `isValidDBusPathSegmentChar` into sdbusplus anyways, so we will need it in that shape as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ACK.  I'm not that worried about this, but I still think inverting the check would be easier to read, but agree to disagree.  THis is fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Rather than sanitizing, should we just be returning an error?  Nobody should be specifying dbus interface names that are invalid and expect them to sanitize correctly.  This is different than dbus paths where we have to take freeform text and convert them into a valid dbus path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I feel like that's something which should be done at the earliest stage of config parsing for `Type` field. No need to run for a while and then found out later that `Type` field is wrong.\n\nWith this patch i try to make a more optimal version of the existing code.\n\nI assume that discussion about right/wrong of existing behavior might be out of scope for a simple optimization change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> I feel like that's something which should be done at the earliest stage of config parsing for `Type` field. No need to run for a while and then found out later that `Type` field is wrong.\n\nTechnically it's enforced at CI build time?  That's about as early as we can get?\n\n> \n> With this patch i try to make a more optimal version of the existing code.\n> \n> I assume that discussion about right/wrong of existing behavior might be out of scope for a simple optimization change.\n\nThis doesn't appear to be optimization, it appears to be new behavior?  Where did we sanitize before?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dbus_util.cpp",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> This doesn't appear to be optimization, it appears to be new behavior?  Where did we sanitize before?\n\nSee the diff of the functions i am replacing.\n\nAnyways i noticed it's just one call site so there is no scope creep to just insert some error handling there like you suggested \ud83d\udc4d"
                }
            ],
